      <activity id="ea3b7462-eabc-5e41-abec-8bc94535c5da" activityNameId="2b78e402-7132-5d20-a5b1-63bda47e50c2" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, PEM, allocated by exergy, distributed  [6b8fe67242]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, PEM, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipeline, produced by Electrolysis, SOEC with steam input using electricity from grid
This dataset represents the supply of 1 kilowatt hour of electricity in a residence, by hydrogen conversion in a fuel cell, PEM. The hydrogen is produced by  Electrolysis, SOEC with steam input, with electricity from grid as feedstock. Electricity conversion efficiency [% LHV input]: 45%. LHV [kWh/kg]: 33.33. Market price [Euro/MJ]: 0.03. Synthesis efficiency [% LHV input]: 0%. Total cap. Input-related [kW]: 2.74. CO2 biogenic share [%]: 0%. Power [kW]: 1.6. Lifetime [years]: 4.88. Annual operation [hours]: 4100. Allocation factor: 0.88. On-site storage loss [%]: 0. Use loss [%]: 0.56. For more information, refer to: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023. Source: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: ab9f4f6c-4c71-3da2-aafb-e6aef59e0ed8
